      "text": "Epilepsy clinic letter\nConsultation: 10 January 2025\nPatient: George Taylor, aged 38\n\nDear colleague,\n\nGeorge attended our outpatient service. He has an established diagnosis of genetic generalized epilepsy with typical absence seizures.\n\nHe describes recurring daytime absence episodes characterized by brief staring and eyelid fluttering lasting 5 to 10 seconds, occurring approximately once or twice daily. His latest absence spell occurred yesterday, 9 January 2025. He reports no generalized convulsions or myoclonic jerks. He continues sodium valproate 500 mg twice daily.\n\nWe agreed to maintain his valproate dose. No EEG requested today. Follow-up in four months.\n"
    }
  ],
